    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 147,
        "text": "Hi Lisa, thanks for meeting me. I wanted to talk about the community garden project. We need to decide how to spend the small grant we received.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "294829f79abe1d62a6c3532023c2f2dd22dfa78c257b16483c26ed18f3a194b8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 151,
        "sourceEnd": 314,
        "text": "Sure, Tom. I’ve looked at the numbers. The grant is £2,000. If we buy seeds and tools, that’s about £500. But we also need to fix the fence, which could cost £800.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "687dfd12a4626b16199298f8d2b7bf5cda98fd019df2d417babfe8a3fe052a72",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 318,
        "sourceEnd": 486,
        "text": "Right. So if we fix the fence first, we’ll have £1,200 left for everything else. But do we really need to fix the whole fence? Maybe we can just repair the broken part.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "440a9157dd811de5669aef9a241d67043987f37a5014658f809ca04055192fff",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 490,
        "sourceEnd": 671,
        "text": "That’s a good point. A partial repair might cost only £300. Then we’d have more for plants. However, if we don’t fix the whole fence, we might have problems with animals getting in.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "00f841217e8bc0065fb0d660d765e84f01e79bfec29d92ab4e601613e1cfc727",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 675,
        "sourceEnd": 828,
        "text": "True. But we could use some of the money for a small tool shed instead. A shed would protect our tools, and it could also store seeds. What do you think?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "a81a5f34afe11f17d02e2ec1b79eff69da442b0a10ee20f44ef453e24ee142bf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 832,
        "sourceEnd": 984,
        "text": "I see your point, but a shed is expensive—at least £600. And we already have a lockable cupboard in the community centre. So maybe we don’t need a shed.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "785fca091727b47e25221b7e2c4bc6d8ac7ec33dbcafc339d3651e083cb8c68d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 988,
        "sourceEnd": 1130,
        "text": "Okay, that makes sense. So what about buying plants? We could buy young plants instead of seeds. They’re more expensive, but they grow faster.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "acea40e67afa4dfad19dcda7930d81549de3996063a100a2dbee2d02aafb7ffd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1134,
        "sourceEnd": 1334,
        "text": "Yes, young plants cost about £200 more than seeds. But if we want a quick harvest, they might be worth it. Although, seeds are more educational for the children—they can see the whole growing process.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "0939ee03c6c89f2cfe8fdb0557ec9c1e63621c772df767fe7aa1a8d90bdd69fb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1338,
        "sourceEnd": 1505,
        "text": "Hmm. Since the project is partly for local schools, maybe we should buy seeds. The children can learn about planting. But then we need to spend more on tools for them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "8735c8014df6015a806c7388be3cb58911612437ccf299b1841f7f963f7c6995",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1509,
        "sourceEnd": 1672,
        "text": "Exactly. So if we buy seeds, we should also buy child-sized tools. That’s an extra £150. But it’s a good investment because the schools might contribute next year.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "2791861b9d7b8bbf0d1c48ebbdbb89f2c875e3babe385ed8f667f267112cb219",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1676,
        "sourceEnd": 1841,
        "text": "I agree. So let’s decide: fix the broken part of the fence for £300, buy seeds for £200, and child-sized tools for £150. That totals £650. We still have £1,350 left.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "fffa6068280c772b92245b65fbdd2f12bbfe8f395a3a569a0ecab30d4d0bc09e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1845,
        "sourceEnd": 2012,
        "text": "Wait, we also need to think about water. The water bill last year was £400. If we install a water butt to collect rain, it costs £250, but then we save on water bills.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "2a87eaa2b6938d6982dbca16e48644ec0d1619b600a9f1f893704a6ce8f24757",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 2016,
        "sourceEnd": 2143,
        "text": "That’s a good idea. A water butt would pay for itself in about two years. But we need to check if we’re allowed to install one.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "70a5013897bc06502f13399359138f06830063f683413763f5a71935ba6e3c0b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 2147,
        "sourceEnd": 2240,
        "text": "I already asked the council. They said yes, as long as it’s not too tall. So we can go ahead.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "75fba3c8321046b56a57a6e4ffee46ae5de2efed2abc359fdd997f9c62f8e345",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 2244,
        "sourceEnd": 2356,
        "text": "Great. So let’s include the water butt. That brings our total to £900. We have £1,100 left for unexpected costs.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "9ae04d4faf5c1aab10d7bb7fdb24c7535fa48e362b3103a031490edf43e3ff22",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 2360,
        "sourceEnd": 2421,
        "text": "Perfect. I’ll write up the plan and send it to the committee.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "3a36c1bdd970d91895eb0caf975000aa03f33dfd892bd53ac8243af7b2dbeacf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
